<title>CANADA: Canadian canola oil disposition forecast to 2000.</title>
<headline>Canadian canola oil disposition forecast to 2000.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Oilseed Processors Association forecast Monday the disposition of canola oil in the year 2000, in thousands of tonnes.</p>
<p>	     CANOLA OILS DISPOSTIONS 1995 VS 2000 ('000 tonnes)</p>
<p>		     1995   FORECAST 2000</p>
<p>North America    1,018  1,175-1,450</p>
<p>  Canada	     646    600-650</p>
<p>  U.S.A.	     365    550-750</p>
<p>  Mexico		 7     25--50</p>
<p>Asia		    49    160-465</p>
<p>  Japan		 11     50-150</p>
<p>  Korea		  3     10--15</p>
<p>  China/Hong Kong   35    100-300</p>
<p>Asia Sub-Continent   2     50--80</p>
<p>Africa/Middle East   3     25</p>
<p>South America	  4     10</p>
<p>Other		    3	0</p>
<p>Total:	     1,079  1,420-2,030</p>
<p>COPA consists of Archer Daniels Midland Co, CanAmera Foods, Canbra Foods Ltd with crush data also provided by  Cargill Ltd, the Canadian unit of Minnesota-based Cargill Inc.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548))</p>
</text>
